  "question": {
    "text": "The instantaneous velocity of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;of the given rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in the represented direction. What is the angular velocity (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) of the rod for the minimum possible magnitude of the velocity of the end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>? \r&nbsp; <img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0071_6809d5c56486.png\" style=\"height: 117px; width: 240px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5.2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "If rod is rotated about end A, then vertical component of velocity, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>⊥</mo></mrow></msub></math> of end a will be zero.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0071_25ebe901c082.png\" style=\"height: 112px; width: 240px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5.2</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"
  }
